A||N||8||DisfourDan||can an Aero nose fit on a 1985 Fiero SE ?||||1||
Z||000000||DisfourDan||06-23-2001||10:42 PM||||I was looking in the Fiero Store catalog, and noticed that the Aero nose was only for the 1986-1988 models.  Can you get them for 1985 Fiero SE?<P>------------------<BR>Nothing good can come from good.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Devotshka||06-23-2001||10:44 PM||||The nose you want was used on:<BR>1984 Indy's<BR>1985 GTs<BR>1986-1987 SEs.<P>The 1986-1988 GT model will fit, but the mouldings will be rounded, instead of ribbed, like your '85 SE.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DisfourDan:<BR><B>I was looking in the Fiero Store catalog, and noticed that the Aero nose was only for the 1986-1988 models.  Can you get them for 1985 Fiero SE?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DisfourDan||06-23-2001||10:46 PM||||is that bad or good?  <P>thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||06-23-2001||10:46 PM||||All the noses will fit any of the cars.  The aero noses were stock on the Indy, 85 GT, 86-87 SE and 86-88 GT.  You just have to make sure that the molding on the nose you get matches what is on your car.<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 06-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||DisfourDan||06-23-2001||10:47 PM||||cool, thanks for the speedy replies.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Devotshka||06-23-2001||10:49 PM||||Assuming you mean the rounded moulding not matching your ribbed moulding, i'd call that bad.  Unless of course you are going for the i-just-bolted-this-part-on look.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Any of the 84 indy/85gt/86-7 se noses will have the correct moulding for your car.  You will need to replace your inner fender (splash-guard thingy) as the aero nose requires a larger one than coupes for proper fit.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DisfourDan:<BR><B>is that bad or good? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||WampusCat||06-23-2001||11:00 PM||||You can change the molding pretty easy.  Though they don't have it listed in their catalog, the Fiero Store has used molding for the aero nose in either round or grooved for about $5 a side.||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||06-24-2001||03:06 AM||||You will also need to drill a hole for the nose badge as the indy/GT/Fiero badges have a different pattern to them.||||reg||1
Z||000008||pontiacs4me||06-24-2001||04:01 PM||||I have an 87 coupe that sports a 1985 gt's aero nose.  My 87 coupe has round moulding and the nose had ribbed.  The rear sections of the moulding are built into the nose.  The marker light section and front arent built in.  I used the 87 marker lights, cut to fit, and I used short strand fiberglass body filler to smooth out the mouldings.  They look fine.||||reg||1
